<title>USA: Guess Inc Q4 pro forma shr $0.28 vs $0.22.</title>
<headline>Guess Inc Q4 pro forma shr $0.28 vs $0.22.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr		 $0.28		    $0.22</p>
<p> Net		 11,871		   9,385</p>
<p> Revs		139,258		  123,952</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  42,682		   42,682</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr		 $1.23		    $1.01</p>
<p> Net		 52,324		   43,287</p>
<p> Revs		551,162		  486,733</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  42,682		   42,682</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE:1996 results include a one-time after-tax reorganization charge of $2.1 million, or $0.05 a share in conjunction with its initial public offering on October 23.</p>
<p>NOTE: Pro forma adjustments include the elimination of certain expenses in connection with the public offering and include a provision for income taxes at an approximate rate of 40 percent, as prior to its IPO, the company was an S corporation and not subject to federal taxes.</p>
